  "promotion": "Each promoted file was rewritten with starter names and structure from the staging copy (never copied whole); \"target\" is the repo file it became, \"stagedTarget\" the path in the staging folder, so the repo file hash differs from stagedSha256. Rewritten to the phase 3 contract: three switchable modes (Auth:Modes basic|ad|sso) on the one session issuer; the generic Codelab.Identity OIDC provider instead of a vendor-specific client; every value that crosses a request (the pending sign-in cookie, the exchange ticket) is a Codelab.Security sealed one-time ticket instead of a signed JWT; the ticket travels in the URL fragment; the per-sign-in cookie named after the state is kept; the ticket-binding cookie became an optional SPA-held binding secret (the SPA calls the API cross-origin without credentials). Left behind on purpose: national-id and OTP login, the gateway SSO mode (phase 8), the logout-hint delivery modes and their table, the feature-flag switch, the source product roles and every vendor name.",
